WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.116
There are a
lot of ways to find content on your site.

00:00:03.116 --> 00:00:07.133
One way is to just find it
on the front end like a user would.

00:00:08.366 --> 00:00:12.216
If you're looking for a news item
that was, created recently,

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:15.416
you can find it in the news list.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.583
Another way is to just search for it
on the front end.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.150
And we can find it there.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.150
Another way is to go to your dashboard

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.600
and each of these blocks,
you know, we have on the news block.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.900
The events block, the media block.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.500
If you click down at the bottom, one more,

00:00:39.866 --> 00:00:42.383
you're going to get all the news

00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:45.383
and you can search it as well.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.716
Now, if all else fails,
the most powerful way

00:00:53.716 --> 00:00:57.650
to, find content is to go to content.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.700
And this is the content management
overview.

00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:05.600
You can see that
we have several different, tabs

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.900
where we can narrow down on, on content,
or we can search for it right here.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.800
We can sort

00:01:14.816 --> 00:01:16.800
newest, oldest.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.366
We can look for stuff that's unpublished.

00:01:19.366 --> 00:01:21.200
We can look for stuff by content type.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.716
So if I only want to departments

00:01:24.716 --> 00:01:28.350
that contain admin,
there's the administration department.
